Excalibur is a lawful artifact, and as such, it will blast anyone who 
isn't lawful. Are you sure you were lawful when you were blasted? From 
reading the spoilers, it seems you can also be blasted when you have 
negative alignment. Did you do anything bad lately, like killing your 
pet or annoying your god?

> 2.    May this character wish for, obtain, and become expert with 
> Grayswandir-and is the weapon really better than Exaclibur ?

You can wish for it (this won't always work), or sacrifice and get it as 
a gift (this might take a while). A Valkyrie can only get to basic in 
silver saber, but that doesn't really matter. Grayswandir is better, 
especially when highly enchanted, but Excalibur is also a really good 
weapon. Don't put too much effort in getting Grayswandir when you 
already have Excalibur.

> 3.    Are blessed fire-proof speed boots obtained by wishing also 
> rot-proof ?

Yes. Currently, fooproof means everything-proof.

> 4.    I seem to get the blame when my rather handy pet Zippo, a fire 
> elemental, incinerates priests or shopkeepers. Is this inevitable-or 
> even true ? And can Zippo increase his HP etc ?

This is not true. The kill appears on the killed monster list at the end 
of the game, but you don't get experience from it, and no negative 
effects occur.

Pets can increase their HP by killing, up to a certain maximum. After 
that, they can only gain HP (levels) by magical means.

